            <ArticleTitle>[Rupture of splenic artery aneurysm as a cause of acute abdomen].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>359-62</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A male, 52 years old, presenting acute abdominal pain and hypovolemic shock, was diagnosed by ultrasound and CAT of fissured aneurysm of the splenic artery. Emergency laparotomy confirmed that the aneurysm had ruptured into the peritoneal cavity.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
